<p>This is definitely neat and gives me a few different concepts to think about.</p>
<p>A. The Time Loop<br />
When Igashi's team goes into a new loop, they don't realize it until exposed to WAN or Jones. Conceptually, this gives me the idea that they've transitioned into a digital world upon entry into the bunker, and that the structure was meant to contain WAN and prevent it from causing chaos upon the world in a breach.</p>
<p>B. Observers<br />
Jones and WAN definitely remind me of two specific characters. In the game Warframe, a digital entity known as Cephalon Suda works to observe, curious about all, and tries to bring people in to her cause. Jones, likewise, brings people in and enlightens them to the cause the Church is working towards. Similarly, WAN is reminiscent of Cephalon Simaris, constantly wanting to assimilate others into it's perfect, digital world.</p>
<p>C. The Messiah<br />
The Questionable part of this comes from Igashi, in that Igashi is just a regular Foundation researcher who, by the look of things, has been amnesticized multiple times. Igashi understands that the horrors of the Foundation are a required sacrifice to better humanity. However WAN and Jones slowly convince Igashi that those necessary horrors aren't required. Something feels off, whether it being that Igashi is anomalously linked to WAN or in that WAN has a charismatic, unavoidable memetic effect.</p>

